<title>PORTUGAL: Trade in Somague, A.Silva suspended - dealers.</title>
<headline>Trade in Somague, A.Silva suspended - dealers.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trade in shares of Portuguese civil engineering group Somague and building firm A.Silva &amp; Silva was suspended on Lisbon bourse by the Financial Markets Committee (CMVM), dealers said.</p>
<p>Reasons for the suspension were not immediately known. CMVM and Lisbon bourse officials were not immediately available.</p>
<p>Publico newspaper reported today that the two companies had reached an agreement for the purchase by Somague of A.Silva &amp; Silva's building subsidiary Assiconstroi for 10.3 billion escudos.</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom +351-1-3538254</p>
</text>
